 "why": "D01/D29 right side: continuous row of 1-bay shops (~2.7 m openings, steel frames) whose thresholds step down with the stepped street (D01), under striped awnings at stepped heights (D01, D29); 2 storeys of ashlar above with sparse small rectangular windows (louvred shutter, grilles), AC units and a glazed box (D01 top right); the street front reads ~13 m against people (1.7 m) in D01. The footprint climbs 6 m up to Sheikh Lulu, so the height is set from the street frontage e19 (eg -22.76): 6.9 m above the highest vertex = 12.9 m above the square. The 26.8 m frontage falls 2.7 m: each bay's door starts at the paving in front of it and has its own awning (gen_overrides fit_slope).",
